<title>UK: Amstrad up on 57.5 mln stg court victory.</title>
<headline>Amstrad up on 57.5 mln stg court victory.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Amstrad Plc rose in pre-market trading on Monday after the consumer electronics group late Friday won damages of 57.5 million stg in a High Court action against disk drive maker Seagate Technology Inc .</p>
<p>The stock was up 26p at 247-1/2 by 0715 GMT in volume of 302,500 shares.  </p>
<p>The award applied to disk drives supplied to Amstrad in the late 1980s for the UK firm's range of business computers.</p>
<p>Amstrad is also taking action against Western Digital Corp, again for alleged problems with disk drives. However, it will not receive the settlement from Seagate immediately, pending the U.S. company's decision on whether to appeal.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
